sanctioned: Ipe types Uuid.v4 / Uuid.v7 on the EFFECT tier (() -> Task Error String) because entropy is not a memoizable pure value (task #54) — this makes "entropy typed as a pure String" unrepresentable. The Go reference still types them as bare `Uuid.v4 : String` (Limitation #7), so this Task-sequenced program is not co-typable with the Go backend and cannot be Go-oracled; Ipe records its own (semantically correct) output "ok". Uuid.parse remains the pure String -> Maybe String parser on both backends.
